WEBVTT

s1-owner-create
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:25.150
Sam, the club Owner, opens Athletes and adds Jordan Avery. Next to the public identity — name, gender, nationality — Owners and Admins can record private contact and eligibility details: an email address, a phone number, and notes. They are labeled private, and FliHub enforces that on the server, not just in the interface.

s2-viewer-readonly
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:46.380
Val is a Viewer in the same organization. She sees Jordan's identity — name, nationality, status — but no email, no phone, no eligibility notes, and no editing controls. Those fields are not hidden in the page; they are never sent to her browser at all.

s3-archive-restore
00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:59.730
Back as the Owner: archiving keeps the record and marks it inactive — there is no permanent delete in this phase. Restoring brings the same record back, details intact.

s4-csv-import
00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:11.490
And for whole rosters, the CSV import adds athletes in bulk — one per row — instead of one form at a time.
